description:
[narrowed from memorynote-write-stores-the-rendered-instruction-envelope-instead-of-the-content-value] A terminal memoryNote_write persists the RENDERED INSTRUCTION as the note body instead of the content value, so a correct answer is stored in a form that fails every byte-equality check. Measured 2026-09-20 with three deterministic probes dispatched back to back. Each note was created within ~30s at the correct title, and each contained the CORRECT arithmetic, wrapped: priorprobe-p1 body = 'memoryNote_write: {
  "title": "priorprobe-p1",
  "content": 106481
}' where the goal asked for 233*457=106481. Same shape for p2 (71219, goal 311*229) and p3 (91337, goal 149*613). Capability is 3/3; the artifact is 0/3. goal-host's own transform-oracle (index.ts:3575) byte-checks a named note with nb.trim() === dtExpected and therefore CANNOT pass any of these, and the standing trend expectation uses the same comparison, so this defect alone pins the deterministic battery at 0/3 regardless of reach.

